{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1765"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/pop-rock","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/music-stage__pop-rock.g4.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",78],["-","Five"],["+","A"],["=",1],["+","handful "],["=",768],["+","Modern pop keeps the guessing game alive. Taylor Swift's \"We Are Never Ever Getting Back Together\", released on 13 August 2012 as the first single from \"Red\" and her first number one on the Billboard Hot 100, is a breezy kiss-off to an ex who keeps coming back. Swift has never named him, but the press reported that the song was about the actor Jake Gyllenhaal, whom she had dated in 2010 and 2011.\n\n"],["=",119],["+","\n| We Are Never Ever Getting Back Together | 2012 | reportedly Jake Gyllenhaal |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",74],["-","Fünf"],["+","Einige"],["=",743],["+","Der moderne Pop hält das Ratespiel am Leben. Taylor Swifts „We Are Never Ever Getting Back Together“, am 13. August 2012 als erste Single aus „Red“ erschienen und ihre erste Nummer eins in den Billboard Hot 100, ist eine flotte Abfuhr an einen Ex, der immer wieder zurückkommt. Swift hat ihn nie genannt, doch die Presse berichtete, der Song handle vom Schauspieler Jake Gyllenhaal, mit dem sie 2010 und 2011 zusammen war.\n\n"],["=",119],["+","\n| We Are Never Ever Getting Back Together | 2012 | angeblich Jake Gyllenhaal |"]]}]},
